From 40a20c40e884d2807471c51e493fac36dbc2dc68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:33:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] dos: Count HSDir requests from relays known only by
 descriptor

HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop refuses an onion service directory request
whose previous hop is neither in our consensus nor a relay whose
descriptor we still hold, as we do for up to two days after it leaves
the consensus. Relays that the directory authorities drop therefore stay
"known" for that long. Before tightening the rule, an operator needs to
know how much traffic comes from them.

Split the lookup that allow_hs_dir_request() already makes into its two
cases, and count the requests whose previous hop is known only by its
descriptor as
tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_descriptor_only_prev_hop"}.
hsdir_unknown_prev_hop keeps its meaning, and what
HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop refuses doesn't change.

Part of #41339.
